Explanation of Changes:

config/config.go (SaveConfig):

The role Role parameter is removed.
It now strictly requires configPath to be non-empty.
It saves the provided cfg *Config to the exact configPath.
install.go (Run function):

Accepts currentCfg *config.Config (the one loaded by Viper in main.go) and roleToInstall config.Role.
It makes a deep copy of currentCfg to configToSave so modifications don't affect main.go's cfg until the installer successfully completes.
It determines the targetSavePath by combining the role-specific data directory (config.GetAppDataDir(selectedRole)) and the role-specific filename (e.g., dev_config.json).
It calls config.SaveConfig(targetSavePath, configToSave) (without the role parameter).
It now returns the configToSave object so main.go can use the configuration that was just installed/updated.
A cliWalletPath parameter is added to installer.Run to allow overriding the default wallet save path during installation if the -wallet_path flag is used.
main.go:

A new flag -wallet_path is added, primarily for the installer to know if a custom wallet save location is desired.
When the installer is run, main.go passes the cfg object (loaded by Viper) to installer.Run.
After the installer runs, main.go updates its cfg variable with the one returned by the installer. This ensures main.go proceeds with the configuration that was just written to the role-specific file.
The explicit config reload after installation in main.go is removed because the installer now returns the up-to-date config object.
This approach ensures that:

Viper loads configuration by trying default_config.json then [role]_config.json.
The installer, when run, always saves its output to the correct [role]_config.json file in the appropriate directory for that role.
main.go uses the configuration that the installer has just set up.
The root role's config (root_config.json) will be saved in the executable's directory, as GetAppDataDir(Root) returns ".".